{
  "english": "Money leaves an account and comes back to it within 7 days, through 2 to 5 transfers. Every hop moves nearly the same amount (within 20% of the previous hop) with patient gaps (fully true to 1 day, false by 5 days). All conditions must hold; fire at 0.5.",
  "motif": "term patient = trapezoid(0h, 0h, 24h, 120h)\n\nmotif cand {\n  match (a:account) -[e:transfer*2..5]-> (a:account)\n  where e is time_ordered and span(e) <= 7d\n  soft each e: e.gap is patient and each e: e.amount ~= prev.amount within 20%\n  score min\n  emit when score >= 0.5\n}\n",
  "narrative": "On 2022-09-03 15:36Z $717.79 moved from 0119/811C597B0 to 0222/811B83280, then on 2022-09-05 06:54Z $703.36 moved from 0222/811B83280 to 0048309/811C599A0, then on 2022-09-06 13:44Z $745.36 moved from 0048309/811C599A0 to 0119/811C597B0 over 2.9d from first to last. The gap after hop 1 was 39.3h and the gap after hop 2 was 30.8h, with each e: gap is patient holding at degree 0.841 and each e: amount ~= prev.amount within 20% holding at degree 0.718. The weakest step is hop 3, where each e: amount ~= prev.amount within 20% holds at 0.718. This returns to 0119/811C597B0 to close the loop.",
  "narrative_anchor_tid": 2012559,
